    "repo": "swesmith/msiemens__tinydb.10644a0e",
    "problem_statement": "Context manager doesn't close storage properly\n\nWhen using TinyDB with a context manager, the storage is not being closed properly when exiting the context. This causes issues with file-based storages where data might not be flushed to disk.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.storages import JSONStorage\nfrom tinydb.middlewares import CachingMiddleware\n\n# Create a temporary database file\npath = 'test.db'\nwith TinyDB(path, storage=CachingMiddleware(JSONStorage)) as db:\n    db.insert({'key': 'value'})\n\n# Check if file was written properly\nstatinfo = os.stat(path)\nprint(f\"File size: {statinfo.st_size}\")  # Should not be 0\nprint(f\"Storage closed: {db._storage._handle.closed}\")  # Should be True\n\n# Try to read the data back\nwith TinyDB(path, storage=CachingMiddleware(JSONStorage)) as db:\n    data = db.all()\n    print(f\"Data: {data}\")  # Should contain the inserted record\n```\n\nThe file size remains 0 and the storage handle is not properly closed, indicating that the data was never flushed to disk when exiting the context manager."
  },
